jzmmc: do not fail data-less commands on stale data error bits

The data error bits in the MSC status register (read timeout, data CRC)
are sticky. After one failed CMD53 they stayed set, and check_error_status()
then failed every following command, including CMD52 register accesses that
carry no data at all. One bad transfer turned into a flood of
"Error status" failures.

Only the response error bits (TIME_OUT_RES, CRC_RES_ERR) can belong to a
command without data, so mask the rest out when host->data is NULL.

Applies on top of 0100-jzmmc-ignore-stale-error-irq.patch.

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/jzmmc_v12.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/jzmmc_v12.c
@@ -313,7 +313,18 @@
 }
 static inline int check_error_status(struct jzmmc_host *host, unsigned int status)
 {
-	if (status & ERROR_STAT) {
+	unsigned int emask = ERROR_STAT;
+
+	/*
+	 * The data error bits in STAT are sticky: a read timeout or data CRC
+	 * error from an earlier CMD53 stays set until the next data transfer.
+	 * A command without data (CMD52) must only be failed by its own
+	 * response errors, otherwise every following CMD52 fails too.
+	 */
+	if (!host->data)
+		emask &= 0x22;	/* TIME_OUT_RES | CRC_RES_ERR */
+
+	if (status & emask) {
 		dev_err(host->dev, "Error status->0x%08X: cmd=%d, state=%d\n",
 			status, host->cmd->opcode, host->state);
 		return -1;
